From a90923a72f95b8e4125af5973c15484ad8afc467 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: William Floyd <git@notmy.space>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 16:48:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ipa: soft: awb: Optionally estimate the illuminant with an
 ONNX model

A tuning's model: key names an ONNX model that takes the statistics' zones
(1 x 3 x 24 x 32, the means above black over full scale) and the gain or
the lux index, and gives the illuminant's R/G and B/G, which stand in for
grey world's before the fit to the locus. The inputs, the output and their
types are checked when it loads, and anything else leaves grey world in
place. Built with the softisp-awb-onnx option, which needs onnxruntime.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
